
"smart_sources:2026-04-19 - Abortion on the ballot in Idaho_ Organizers are ‘confident’ initiative qualified.md": {"path":"2026-04-19 - Abortion on the ballot in Idaho_ Organizers are ‘confident’ initiative qualified.md","last_embed":{"hash":null},"embeddings":{},"last_read":{"hash":"1d611ol","at":1785795032201},"class_name":"SmartSource","last_import":{"mtime":1783529619126,"size":6789,"at":1785795032306,"hash":"1d611ol"},"blocks":{"#---frontmatter---":[1,9],"#":[10,29],"##Ballot proposal would restore abortion access, protect contraception and more":[30,60],"##Ballot proposal would restore abortion access, protect contraception and more#{1}":[32,60]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Nicole Blanchard","target":"Nicole Blanchard","line":5},{"title":"A sign outside the Idaho Capitol gives information on the Reproductive Freedom and Privacy Act, a citizen-led ballot initiative in response to Idaho's ban on abortion.","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/public/latest-news/fnwt3t/picture314361635/alternates/LANDSCAPE_1200/BOI_011703womensmarch.JPG","line":10,"embedded":true},{"title":"a proposed ballot initiative","target":"https://sos.idaho.gov/elections/initiatives/2026/RFPA.pdf","line":16},{"title":"Idahoans United for Women and Families","target":"https://iduwf.org/","line":18},{"title":"Melanie Folwell, executive director of Idahoans United for Women & Families, speaks on the steps of the Idaho Capitol Building during the annual Women's March, Saturday, Jan. 17, 2026. Folwell spoke about the Reproductive Freedom and Privacy Act, a citizen-led ballot initiative in response to Idaho's ban on abortion.","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/public/latest-news/3644mp/picture314361632/alternates/FREE_1200/BOI_011705womensmarch.JPG","line":26,"embedded":true},{"title":"Boise State University","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/news/politics-government/state-politics/article314433069.html","line":40},{"title":"Idahoans United for Women and Families supporters pose with signs bearing slogans urging an end to Idaho’s abortion ban. The group is behind the ballot initiative that would carve out the right to abortion until fetal viability, as well as rights to contraception, fertility treatment and other reproductive health care.","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/public/latest-news/gucgjw/picture315447047/alternates/FREE_1200/IMG_5598.JPG","line":46,"embedded":true},{"title":"after suing","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/news/politics-government/state-politics/article299529039.html","line":50},{"title":"ruled in the nonprofit’s favor","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/news/politics-government/state-politics/article308784295.html","line":52}],"metadata":{"title":"Abortion on the ballot in Idaho? Organizers are ‘confident’ initiative qualified","source":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/news/politics-government/state-politics/article315437967.html#campaignName=boise_politics_newsletter","author":["[[Nicole Blanchard]]"],"published":"2026-04-19","created":"2026-07-08","description":"The proposal would restore abortion access and carve out rights to other reproductive care, like birth control and fertility treatment."},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[]},